  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the textual metaphor",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the textual material 'they are like sperm you get millions, but only one works' because the meme uses second-person address implicitly. The phrase 'you get millions' and 'only one works' directly addresses the viewer, making the user feel personally implicated in the metaphorical judgment being applied to the crowd. The user is invited to identify with the perspective of the speaker, who is dehumanizing the crowd (likely immigrants or refugees) by comparing them to sperm. This projection makes the user feel like they are the one making the judgment or the one who must choose 'the one that works' from the 'millions'.",
